    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363-a4">

                <pb facs="0845" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg749"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 849.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pigeon to Mr.
                            Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Luis Potosi</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 30,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Friend</hi>: My father, Mr. Eugene Pigeon, has
                    requested me to write to you and entreat you to inform him with regard to an
                    extraordinary tax which must be paid. It is truly and really a very
                    extraordinary tax, being 9¾ per cent, on the profits, which all the commerce of
                    this city refuses to pay, and in virtue thereof has asked amparo at
                    Guanajuato.</p>
                <p>We would desire to know, as American citizens, whether we are compelled to pay
                    such contributions.</p>
                <p>Please be kind enough to inform us immediately by telegraph or by letter at Libro
                    Mayor.</p>
                <p>Receive beforehand our most sincere thanks for the many favors we permit
                    ourselves to trouble you with.</p>
                <p>Hoping soon to hear from you, I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>RUDOLPH PIGEON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
